# Python quality gates

After implementing or changing Python code, run all four tools on the affected paths before considering the work done. Fix failures; do not skip a tool.

```bash
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
pytest
ty check
pylint app tests
```

## Rules

- Run them after the implementation, not instead of writing tests.
- Scope to the files you touched when a full-repo run is too broad (`ruff check path`, `pylint path`, `pytest path`).
- If a tool is missing from the environment, install/configure it in the project rather than skipping it.
- Do not add `# noqa`, `# type: ignore`, or pylint disables to silence new issues unless the reason is documented in the same line.

Work is not complete until all four pass.
